---
import { LINKS } from '../lib/site';

const faqs = [
  {
    q: "Why doesn't the total match Windows' page?",
    a: "Windows shows one network at a time; the dashboard counts them all. Compare Windows' figure with that network's row under Where it went.",
  },
  {
    q: 'How accurate are the numbers?',
    a: "They are Windows' own: checked app by app against its Data usage page, several within a fraction of a percent.",
  },
  {
    q: 'What happens after a Windows reset?',
    a: `The database is on another drive, so it survives. <code>npm run restore</code> and two setup scripts bring the rest back. <a href="${LINKS.recovery}">The steps</a>.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'Does anything leave my PC?',
    a: 'No. Phones post to the dashboard on your network, or optionally through a cloud inbox that cannot read what it carries.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I add a phone and the PC together?',
    a: "Never add the two: a laptop tethered to a phone has counted those bytes already. Each device has its own pages.",
  },
  {
    q: 'Is it free?',
    a: `Yes, under the <a href="${LINKS.license}">MIT license</a>. Bugs and questions go to the <a href="${LINKS.issues}">issue tracker</a>.`,
  },
];
---

<section class="section" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
  <div class="container faq">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">FAQ</p>
      <h2 id="faq-title">Questions, answered.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="list">
      {
        faqs.map((item) => (
          <details>
            <summary>{item.q}</summary>
            <p class="muted" set:html={item.a} />
          </details>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .faq {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .list {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  /* Wide screens: the heading on the left, the questions beside it. */
  @media (min-width: 980px) {
    .faq {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 2fr;
      gap: 64px;
      align-items: start;
    }
  }

  details {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    transition: background-color var(--dur) var(--ease);
  }

  /* Hover: the row lifts onto a surface and the question takes the accent. */
  details:hover,
  details[open] {
    background: var(--surface);
  }

  summary {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 16px;
    padding: 18px 14px;
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
    transition: color var(--dur) var(--ease);
  }

  summary:hover {
    color: var(--accent-bright);
  }

  summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  summary::after {
    content: '+';
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    flex: none;
    width: 28px;
    height: 28px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    color: var(--accent-bright);
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    line-height: 1;
    transition:
      background-color var(--dur) var(--ease),
      box-shadow var(--dur) var(--ease);
  }

  summary:hover::after {
    background: var(--accent-dim);
    box-shadow: 0 0 16px var(--accent-glow);
  }

  details[open] summary::after {
    content: '−';
  }

  details p {
    padding: 0 14px 20px;
  }
</style>
